I think there is an issue here that appears randomly across runs and brings flakiness. After any test marked `@pytest.mark.django_db(transaction=True)` finishes, its teardown truncates every table, and that commit takes the migration-seeded rows with it, including the default `CustomerType`. Nothing puts it back, the database then stays broken for every later run with `--reuse-db`
From that point on, tests that request `default_customer_type` or create a user through `dangerously_create_test_user` are fine, but any test needing the default row without going through either one fails.

19667.body:
Enforces gift card customer assignment in `transactionInitialize`, matching `checkoutAddPromoCode`:

- restricted cards require the assigned authenticated customer and otherwise return a generic error;
- cards backing checkout transactions cannot be reassigned;
- full cancellation releases the card atomically.

Fixes #19612  
[ENG-1746](https://linear.app/saleor/issue/ENG-1746/enforce-gift-card-customer-assignment-in-the-transaction-flow)

